      "pins": ["D7.2", "U3.5", "U4.5", "U5.5", "U10.20"],
      "nets": ["NET0008 (SCK / WS2812B-DIN)"],
      "observed": "On the Microcontroller sheet the WS2812B status LED D7 has its DIN pin wired to net NET0008, and on the Thermocouples sheet the SCK pin (5) of all three MAX31855KASA devices (U3, U4, U5) is also wired to NET0008; on the MCU NET0008 is the GPIO5/SCK output. The SPI clock line and the addressable-LED data line are therefore joined on one net.",
      "expected": "The specification describes a shared SPI SCK bus (SCK tied to the three thermocouple ICs and to ESP32 GPIO5) and a separate single WS2812B status LED (D1) on its own data GPIO. SCK must not be connected to the WS2812B DIN.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Thermocouples sheet: U5/U4/U3 pin 5 'SCK' -> NET0008 (three boxes all labelled NET0008)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Microcontroller sheet (right tile): D7 WS2812B 'DIN' -> NET0008"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "SPI bus is shared across all three chips: SCK (pin 5) ... tied to all three ICs and to the ESP32 (U1 GPIO5/SCK) ... a single onboard WS2812B status LED (D1)."}
      ],
      "impact": "The 60 MHz SPI clock used to poll the thermocouples is driven onto the WS2812B data input, and the LED's data stream is driven onto the thermocouple clock. Both the thermocouple reads and the status LED will be corrupted/non-functional; the ESP32 GPIO5 is also asked to source two unrelated loads.",
      "confidence": 0.7
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["J8", "U10"],
      "pins": ["J8.A7", "J8.A6", "U10.26", "U10.27"],
      "nets": ["NET0014", "NET0009"],
      "observed": "On the Microcontroller sheet the USB-C receptacle J8 D- pin (A7) is wired to NET0014 while the D+ pin (A6) is wired to NET0009; on the ESP32-C3 the same nets are attached to the opposite data pins (NET0014 -> pin 26 GPIO18/USB_D+, NET0009 -> pin 27 GPIO19/USB_D-). The USB differential pair is transposed.",
      "expected": "ESP32 USB_D+ must connect to the connector D+ (A6/B6) and USB_D- to D- (A7/B7); a swapped pair prevents USB enumeration/programming.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Microcontroller sheet: J8 A7 'D-' -> NET0014, A6 'D+' -> NET0009; U10 pin 26 'GPIO18/USB_D+' -> NET0014, pin 27 'GPIO19/USB_D-' -> NET0009"}
      ],
      "impact": "Native USB on the ESP32-C3 will not enumerate, so USB-based programming/serial would fail (the 5 V supply path is unaffected).",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the intended design: the SPI SCK net (NET0008) is bridged onto the WS2812B status-LED data input, corrupting both the thermocouple bus and the LED, and the USB-C D+/D- lines appear transposed at the connector. The power, heater-switch, buck and power-mux sections otherwise match the specification's values and topology."
}

